{"format":"frost-first-consonant-scope-v1","relation_id":"A1","name":"Initial-consonant agreement","definition":{"positive":"For two different word occurrences, their first phonemes are the same consonant under a compatible pair of complete declared pronunciations.","predicate":"first_consonant(a) is not None and first_consonant(a) == first_consonant(b)","negative":"A vowel-initial member, different initial consonants, or phonetic similarity without exact consonant identity fails. A consonant later in a vowel-initial word is not an initial consonant.","unresolved":"Missing or unrecognized pronunciations raise an error; they are never silently recorded as nonmatches.","anchor":"Word-start only, not the first consonant found anywhere and not a relocated stressed-syllable onset.","identity":"Occurrences must differ. Repeated spelling is allowed and reported separately; native E9 instead excludes same-spelling pairs.","stress":"No stress threshold is imposed on this evidence relation. Stress-sensitive figure recognition requires a further declared rule.","distance":"The relation covers all occurrence pairs. A remote match alone is not a claim of a locally salient rhetorical figure. Same-line candidates are supplied without claiming that one line is the universal proximity boundary.","scope":"Annotated uses one existing pinned pronunciation per occurrence; dictionary_union is existential across the existing dictionary alternatives plus already-declared sourced additions. Both yield the same positive pairs here, but their complete-pronunciation witnesses differ.","vowels":"Vowel-initial agreement is excluded. This is a first-consonant relation, not a first-phoneme rule that also accepts matching vowels or an empty-onset rule.","clusters":"Only the first consonant must agree. Complete onset equality remains the stricter native E9. CH/JH are single affricate phones; W/Y are consonantal glides."},"sources":[{"id":"poetry_foundation","url":"https://www.poetryfoundation.org/education/glossary/Alliteration","support":"Defines initial stressed consonant repetition, and explicitly allows different complete initial clusters, illustrated by pizza/place.","retrieval":"Verified in search result; direct page fetch returned 403."},{"id":"american_poets","url":"https://poets.org/glossary/alliteration","support":"Defines grouped words sharing their first consonant sound; its examples include different s-initial clusters."},{"id":"poetry_archive","url":"https://poetryarchive.org/glossary/alliteration/","support":"Requires nearby sound repetition and distinguishes written initials from consonant sounds; admits word-start or first-stressed-syllable anchors. This relation deliberately implements only word-start evidence."}],"source_sha256":{"frost_pair_analysis/annotated_readings.json":"401d4b3f62e3608db0b4047da0c668a3db80799de6d88295c12b17b81df0236c","frost_pair_analysis/frost_annotated_pairs.json":"70ca0a2c0de9f6e18e0bfdfeedcc3d65b16a7d407881c1faad84813d45fbd18d","frost_pair_analysis/frost_rhyme_pairs.json":"c220abd27901c34fca8892c347aeaa48901333da98dcf46d9b653e7e707cac8c","frost_pair_analysis/poem_readings.py":"15314126a3bac6fbd179b5f3bfe688b3a5ef8ee09a1cec902fb17c5dcbe6d689","frost_pair_analysis/english_schema_contracts.py":"4abce7544ef13cb061df6b9116e896c8f42434ae71023c64cfe7280ef93c8de6","frost_pair_analysis/CodexMusica/lyric-harness/quality/relations.py":"a2be3949d5f9368534e1aadc27a29b8c165f4cdb6786b581979ea01ce09227ad"},"pronunciation_columns":["ARPAbet_phone_sequence"],"pronunciations":[["HH","UW1","Z"],["W","UH1","D","Z"],["DH","IY1","Z"],["AA1","R"],["ER0"],["AY1"],["TH","IH1","NG","K"],["N","OW1"],["HH","IH0","Z"],["HH","IH1","Z"],["HH","AW1","S"],["IH0","Z"],["IH1","Z"],["IH1","N"],["IH0","N"],["DH","AH0"],["DH","AH1"],["DH","IY0"],["V","IH1","L","IH0","JH"],["V","IH1","L","AH0","JH"],["DH","OW1"],["HH","IY1"],["W","IH1","L"],["W","AH0","L"],["N","AA1","T"],["S","IY1"],["M","IY1"],["S","T","AA1","P","IH0","NG"],["HH","IY1","R"],["T","AH0"]